**Summary of Decision:**
Redis Streams was selected over Kafka due to the team's size (6 engineers, no dedicated infra), existing production presence of Redis, and the 2-week delivery constraint. While Kafka offers superior durability and scale for massive datasets, Redis Streams comfortably meets the 10x growth target (~5k req/s) with significantly lower operational complexity and a faster time-to-value. Exactly-once semantics for billing will be handled via application-level idempotency.

